module mirror_bare_origin

// mirror_bare_origin.ri — task 5748 (PRD docs/prds/v0_6/check-diagnostic-truthfulness.md, leaf β).
//
// Reproduces the `mirror(...)` bare-origin anti-pattern in its DECODED-VALUE
// form: `plane_yz(0)` takes a bare-Int offset where a dimensioned `0mm` is
// required, so the plane it produces carries a non-Length ox and the geometry
// op fails to compile at realization time.
//
// WHY THIS ROUTE AND NOT THE 7-ARG SCALAR ONE (task 5662).  This fixture's job
// for leaf β is to be a BUILD-ONLY diagnostic — one that `check` can only
// surface by reaching build() — and the 7-arg scalar form no longer qualifies.
// The full argument (why the arity guard is load-bearing, and why the
// decoded-value route is a STRUCTURAL exclusion from the compile slot table) is
// stated once, on the `mirror` / `circular_pattern` arms of `builtin_arg_slots`
// in `crates/reify-compiler/src/builtin_signatures.rs`.  Read it there.
// The fixture stays deliberately BARE either way — only the route changed.
//
// Verified baseline, RE-MEASURED on this file at task 5746 (units-length ε, R11
// — `docs/prds/v0_6/units-length-gate-completion.md`), which is what changed the
// stderr below.  ε requires `plane_yz`'s offset to be a Length, so `plane_yz(0)`
// is now rejected at the PRODUCER and `mirror` never receives a Plane at all:
// the consumer-side ox/oy/oz triple this fixture used to elicit is no longer
// reached on this route, and ONE producer rejection replaces it.  The fixture
// stays deliberately BARE — it is now a test OF that gate.
//
//   reify check <this file>                                          exit 1
//     stdout: "  OK MirrorBareOrigin#constraint[0]"
//             "All constraints satisfied."
//     stderr: error: plane_yz: offset argument expects Length, got Int; pass a
//                    dimensioned length such as `5mm`
//             error: failed to compile geometry operation: mirror: expected a
//                    Plane value, got undef                     [exactly ONCE]
//             error: failed to compile geometry operation: unresolvable
//                    GeomRef::Step(1) — index out of bounds or INVALID handle
//
//   The `expected a Plane value` line is the compile-gate diagnostic the
//   `missing or non-Length argument 'ox'` line used to be, and it inherits the
//   internal duplication that makes the dedup pin load-bearing: `reify eval` and
//   `reify build` on this file were both measured printing it TWICE, while
//   `check` prints it once.
//
// Before leaf β, that stderr was EMPTY — `check` never realized geometry for a
// module carrying no Conforms / RepresentationWithin / DFMRule constraint.  Leaf
// β (D1 geometry routing + D2 build-diagnostic merge) is what makes it truthful,
// and D2's accumulating dedup is what pins the 'ox' line at exactly one
// occurrence.  `check` exits non-zero because `check_gating_error` gates on
// any non-allowlisted Severity::Error in the merged set (#5403), and no
// CHECK_ERROR_EXIT_ALLOWLIST entry covers the plane_yz producer rejection or
// the geometry-compile family — deliberately: they are genuine design errors,
// as `reify eval` agrees.  Asserted by
// cli_check.rs::check_surfaces_geometry_compile_error_from_discarded_build.

structure MirrorBareOrigin {
    param arm_len       : Length = 40mm
    param arm_width     : Length = 8mm
    param arm_thickness : Length = 5mm

    let arm = box(arm_len, arm_width, arm_thickness)

    // WRONG on purpose — bare-Int plane offset (should be `0mm`).
    let reflected = mirror(arm, plane_yz(0))

    param geometry : Solid = union(arm, reflected)

    // Trivially satisfied, so the summary line is "All constraints satisfied."
    // and the ONLY new observable is the geometry-compile diagnostic.
    constraint arm_len > arm_width
}
